{"info":{"author":null,"author_email":"LanceDB Devs <dev@lancedb.com>","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 3 - Alpha","Environment :: Console","Intended Audience :: Science/Research","License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License","Operating System :: OS Independent","Programming Language :: Python","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13","Topic :: Scientific/Engineering"],"description":"# LanceDB Python SDK\n\nA Python library for [LanceDB](https://github.com/lancedb/lancedb).\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install lancedb\n```\n\nIf no wheel is published for your platform, pip builds `lancedb` from the source distribution. That build needs a [Rust toolchain](https://rustup.rs/) and [protoc](https://grpc.io/docs/protoc-installation/) (the Protocol Buffers compiler) on your `PATH`, and can take a while.\n\n### Pre-Haswell x86_64 hosts: `lancedb-compat`\n\nThe default `lancedb` wheel targets `x86-64-haswell` (AVX2 + FMA + F16C) for full performance on modern hardware. Pre-Haswell hosts — Intel Sandy Bridge / Ivy Bridge / Westmere; AMD Bulldozer / Piledriver / Steamroller — don't have AVX2 and crash with `Illegal instruction` at `import lancedb`.\n\nFor those hosts, install the `lancedb-compat` package instead:\n\n```bash\npip install lancedb-compat\n```\n\nSame Python API (`import lancedb` works as usual). The compat wheel is compiled at the `x86-64-v2` baseline (Nehalem-class) and uses runtime SIMD dispatch in the embedded lance crate to pick the right kernel tier (scalar / AVX / AVX+FMA / AVX2+FMA / AVX-512) at load time, so it still goes fast on modern hardware while running cleanly on the pre-Haswell silicon. Use `lance.simd_info()` from Python to verify which tier was selected.\n\n`lancedb` and `lancedb-compat` install to the same `lancedb/` namespace and conflict at install time. Pick one. To switch, `pip uninstall lancedb` first, then `pip install lancedb-compat` (or vice-versa).\n\nIf you need a custom baseline (or `lancedb-compat` isn't yet published for your platform), build from source with the override:\n\n```bash\nRUSTFLAGS=\"-C target-cpu=x86-64-v2\" maturin build --release\npip install ./target/wheels/lancedb-*.whl\n```\n\n### Preview Releases\n\nStable releases are created about every 2 weeks. For the latest features and bug fixes, you can install the preview release. These releases receive the same level of testing as stable releases, but are not guaranteed to be available for more than 6 months after they are released. Once your application is stable, we recommend switching to stable releases.\n\n\n```bash\npip install --pre --extra-index-url https://pypi.fury.io/lancedb/ lancedb\n```\n\nIf you also need the optional `lance` Python API, install the `pylance` extra\nand include the Lance preview index:\n\n```bash\npip install --pre \\\n  --extra-index-url https://pypi.fury.io/lancedb/ \\\n  --extra-index-url https://pypi.fury.io/lance-format/ \\\n  \"lancedb[pylance]\"\n```\n\nWith uv, also select the best matching version across the indexes:\n\n```bash\nuv pip install --prerelease allow \\\n  --index https://pypi.fury.io/lancedb/ \\\n  --index https://pypi.fury.io/lance-format/ \\\n  --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \\\n  \"lancedb[pylance]\"\n```\n\nThe LanceDB preview index contains old `pylance` releases; current Lance previews\nare published to the `lance-format` index. By default, uv only considers versions\nfrom the first index containing a package, which can select an old `pylance` or\nbacktrack to an older LanceDB release. `unsafe-best-match` searches all configured\nindexes, like pip; use it only with indexes you trust. Install the extra rather\nthan an unconstrained `pylance` so LanceDB's minimum supported version is enforced.\n\n### Threading in CPU-limited containers\n\nLanceDB uses separate pools for compute work and storage I/O. On a container with\ntwo visible CPUs, current releases intentionally use one compute worker by default;\nno manual configuration is needed. If every query logs an I/O core reservation\nwarning on a two-CPU container, upgrade from LanceDB 0.21.1 or earlier.\n\nThe two commonly tuned environment variables control different resources:\n\n- `LANCE_CPU_THREADS` overrides the number of compute workers. One worker is the\n  appropriate setting for a two-CPU container when an explicit override is needed.\n- `LANCE_IO_THREADS` controls concurrent storage operations, not reserved CPU\n  cores. Its default can be greater than the number of CPUs because I/O workers\n  spend much of their time waiting for storage.\n\nKeep the defaults unless measurements show that the workload benefits from an\noverride. See the [Lance threading model](https://lance.org/guide/performance/#threading-model)\nfor the current defaults and tuning guidance.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Basic Example\n\n```python\nimport lancedb\ndb = lancedb.connect('<PATH_TO_LANCEDB_DATASET>')\ntable = db.open_table('my_table')\nresults = table.search([0.1, 0.3]).limit(20).to_list()\nprint(results)\n```\n\n### Development\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for information on how to contribute to LanceDB.\n\n### Opening SQL blob descriptors\n\nA SQL `blob_descriptor(video)` result keeps the Blob V2 storage metadata and a\n`source` struct containing its table URI, version, commit timestamp, branch,\ncolumn and row identity. This example uses a remote SQL connection whose SQL\nservice produces those source-bearing descriptors. Open the reference on the\nsource table to read incrementally:\n\n```python\nrows = db.execute_query(\"\"\"\n    SELECT f.timestamp, blob_descriptor(v.video) AS video\n    FROM videos v JOIN frames f ON v.id = f.video_id\n\"\"\").read_all()\n\nvideos = db.open_table(\"videos\")\nfor row in rows.to_pylist():\n    if row[\"video\"] is not None:\n        with videos.open_blob_file(row[\"video\"]) as video:\n            frame = extract_frame(video, row[\"timestamp\"])\n```\n\n`open_blob_file` accepts the dictionary or an Arrow struct scalar directly. It\nkeeps the query's version and branch without changing the table handle's checkout.\nPayload bytes load on reads. An external blob with an unspecified size may need a\nmetadata-only HEAD request to open.\n\n`videos.open_blob_files(rows[\"video\"])` returns an iterator over the same handles,\npreserving order, duplicates and nulls (`None`). It accepts Arrow arrays/chunked\narrays or another iterable and opens each handle as iteration advances. Close each\nnon-null handle after use. Async tables offer `await videos.open_blob_file(...)`\nand `async for video in videos.open_blob_files(...)`.\n\n```python\nfor video in videos.open_blob_files(rows[\"video\"]):\n    if video is not None:\n        with video:\n            header = video.read(4096)\n```\n\nTo extract a frame while retaining each row's timestamp, iterate over the\nhandles and rows together:\n\n```python\nfor row, video in zip(rows.to_pylist(), videos.open_blob_files(rows[\"video\"])):\n    if video is not None:\n        with video:\n            frame = extract_frame(video, row[\"timestamp\"])\n```\n\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown; charset=UTF-8; variant=GFM","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":"data-format, data-science, machine-learning, arrow, data-analytics","license":null,"license_expression":null,"license_files":["LICENSE"],"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"lancedb","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lancedb/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lancedb/","project_urls":{"repository":"https://github.com/lancedb/lancedb"},"provides_extra":["azure","clip","dev","docs","embeddings","otel","pylance","siglip","tests"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lancedb/0.41.0/","requires_dist":["deprecation>=2.1.0","numpy>=1.24.0","overrides>=0.7; python_full_version < \"3.12\"","packaging>=23.0","pyarrow>=16","pydantic<3,>=2.7.4","tqdm>=4.27.0","lance-namespace>=0.13.0","adlfs>=2024.2.0; extra == \"azure\"","torch; extra == \"clip\"","pillow>=12.1.1; extra == \"clip\"","open-clip-torch; extra == \"clip\"","ruff>=0.3.0; extra == \"dev\"","pre-commit>=3.5.0; extra == \"dev\"","pyright>=1.1.350; extra == \"dev\"","typing-extensions>=4.0.0; python_full_version < \"3.11\" and extra == \"dev\"","maturin>=1.10; extra == \"dev\"","mkdocs; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-jupyter; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-material; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocstrings-python; extra == \"docs\"","requests>=2.31.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","openai>=1.6.1; extra == \"embeddings\"","sentence-transformers>=2.2.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","torch>=2.0.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","pillow>=12.1.1; extra == \"embeddings\"","open-clip-torch>=2.20.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","cohere>=4.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","colpali-engine>=0.3.10; extra == \"embeddings\"","huggingface-hub>=0.19.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","instructorembedding>=1.0.1; extra == \"embeddings\"","google-genai>=1.0.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","boto3>=1.28.57; extra == \"embeddings\"","awscli>=1.44.38; extra == \"embeddings\"","botocore>=1.31.57; extra == \"embeddings\"","ibm-watsonx-ai>=1.1.2; python_full_version >= \"3.10\" and extra == \"embeddings\"","ollama>=0.3.0; extra == \"embeddings\"","sentencepiece>=0.1.99; extra == \"embeddings\"","opentelemetry-api; extra == \"otel\"","pylance>=14.0.2; extra == \"pylance\"","torch; extra == \"siglip\"","pillow>=12.1.1; extra == \"siglip\"","transformers>=4.41.0; extra == \"siglip\"","sentencepiece; extra == \"siglip\"","aiohttp>=3.9.0; extra == \"tests\"","boto3>=1.28.57; extra == \"tests\"","pandas>=1.4; extra == \"tests\"","pytest>=7.0; extra == \"tests\"","pytest-mock>=3.10; extra == \"tests\"","pytest-asyncio>=0.21; extra == \"tests\"","duckdb>=0.9.0; extra == \"tests\"","pytz>=2023.3; extra == \"tests\"","polars<=1.32.3,>=0.19; extra == \"tests\"","pyarrow<25; extra == \"tests\"","pyarrow-stubs>=16.0; extra == \"tests\"","pylance==14.0.2; extra == \"tests\"","requests>=2.31.0; extra == \"tests\"","datafusion<55,>=54; extra == \"tests\"","opentelemetry-sdk>=1.30.0; extra == \"tests\""],"requires_python":">=3.10","summary":"lancedb","version":"0.41.0","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":42906481,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"Xuanwo"},{"role":"Owner","user":"changhiskhan"},{"role":"Owner","user":"eddyxu"},{"role":"Owner","user":"jackye1995"},{"role":"Owner","user":"wjones127"},{"role":"Owner","user":"wkalt"}]},"urls":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"1b20c8001a37a98f7db97fc25ba9adc483ad83fdf32d48fc9a49bb44a80e9df6"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"2e17c77b33e6af5c8da320843ead3d2988adbb71b26b731b2fe20d38b1116f5d","md5":"7c6267bc2a7338f84dc94dc63ec3520c","sha256":"b8892ff52eb32224c0414feb6f57357c4b79edeed0c2a4afe6d7f6f538dc12d0"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"lancedb-0.41.0-cp310-abi3-macosx_11_0_arm64.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"7c6267bc2a7338f84dc94dc63ec3520c","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"cp310","requires_python":">=3.10","size":69031230,"upload_time":"2026-10-29T09:10:26","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-10-29T09:10:26.053259Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/2e/17/c77b33e6af5c8da320843ead3d2988adbb71b26b731b2fe20d38b1116f5d/lancedb-0.41.0-cp310-abi3-macosx_11_0_arm64.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"1b20c8001a37a98f7db97fc25ba9adc483ad83fdf32d48fc9a49bb44a80e9df6"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"0432b6b8a41ce5e255078e52405ca0340fc579c378dca0b1cc1fbfb2bcdf1fb2","md5":"1aaa70c69bdf646f646455e41e67e7c2","sha256":"984d97c50169face1539ccaa802a2002ebc7b50a445c3e7e8cd24513569c1aab"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"lancedb-0.41.0-cp310-abi3-manylinux_2_28